<title>USA: NYPA's Fitzpatrick NY nuke begins restart.</title>
<headline>NYPA's Fitzpatrick NY nuke begins restart.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Power Authority's (NYPA) 832 megawatt (MW) James A Fitzpatrick nuclear power plant restarted early this morning, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Wednesday in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Scriba, N.Y., was shut Sunday while in restart mode when a leak was detected in the plant's electrical hydraulic control system.</p>
<p>It typically takes a couple of days to bring a nuclear plant back up to full power production if all goes smoothly.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
</text>
